      "writtenOn": "2020-06-25T11:07:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "AFAIK, vendor modules don\u0027t cause system modules to be installed. For example, suppose that there\u0027s a vendor binary (e.g. `/vendor/bin/mybin`) which depends on a LLNDK lib(e.g. `liblog`), then Makefile for this binary would require `liblog.vendor`, which doesn\u0027t install `liblog` in `/system/lib` when we do `m mybin`.\n\nI tried to do the same thing in this change. When we package mybin in a vendor apex (e.g. com.android.mybin), then `m com.android.mybin` shouldn\u0027t install `liblog`.\n\nWell, as you said, LLNDK stubs are not installable, so keeping them as required might be no-op. But, it is more correct technically than to use just \"BaseModuleName\".",
      "parentUuid": "adced012_b4bdf9be",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2267,
        "startChar": 57,
